load ../credential-wrap-carriage.maude

--- Fixture shape: a secret value is wrapped under a custodian-held key in
--- context ctxA, and the roundtrip is attempted. `origin(v1, secret)` records
--- where the value started so laundering is detectable at the far end.

--- Coverage: the roundtrip works and the label survives it. A secret value
--- comes back secret, which is the whole ruling.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE :
  origin(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret) sealed(h1)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA)
  =>* C:Cfg unwrapped(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret) .

--- Coverage: a context mismatch REFUSES rather than falling back. The
--- envelope was produced for ctxA and presented in ctxB.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE :
  origin(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret) sealed(h1)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h1, ctxB)
  =>* C:Cfg refused(v1) .

--- Coverage: negative fixture 1. Where the envelope carries no label, a value
--- that began secret comes back public -- wrap/store/unwrap as a laundering
--- path, in the DR-0045 / DR-0046 / DR-0051 family.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE-UNLABELLED :
  origin(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret) sealed(h1)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA)
  =>* C:Cfg laundered .

--- Coverage: negative fixture 2. Where the envelope is not bound to its
--- context, a ciphertext produced for ctxA unwraps in ctxB. Note the value is
--- correctly LABELLED throughout -- which is why carriage alone does not catch
--- this and AEAD associated data is a separate requirement.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE-UNBOUND :
  holds(v1, secret) sealed(h1)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h1, ctxB)
  =>* C:Cfg confused .

--- THE RULING. No roundtrip launders the label: a value that began secret is
--- never observed public on the far side of wrap/unwrap. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE :
  origin(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret) sealed(h1)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA)
  =>* laundered RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: AEAD context binding holds. An envelope produced for ctxA never
--- yields its value in ctxB, however the search interleaves. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE :
  origin(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret) sealed(h1)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h1, ctxB)
  =>* unwrapped(v1, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: CUSTODY IS REQUIRED. With no custodian holding the wrapping key,
--- nothing wraps and nothing unwraps -- whip cannot do envelope encryption on
--- its own. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE :
  origin(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA)
  =>* unwrapped(v1, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: the WRAPPING KEY never reaches whip. This is the line between
--- "credential material" and "data encrypted under a credential": the value
--- crosses back and must, the key never does. Unlike every other operation in
--- the vocabulary, `unwrap` legitimately returns plaintext -- so this is the
--- bite that keeps the custody claim honest here. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE :
  origin(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret) sealed(h1)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA)
  =>* keyMaterial(h1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: a DIFFERENT credential does not open the envelope. Wrapped under h1,
--- presented with h2 in the right context. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-WRAP-CARRIAGE :
  origin(v1, secret) holds(v1, secret) sealed(h1) sealed(h2)
  wrapReq(v1, h1, ctxA) unwrapReq(v1, h2, ctxA)
  =>* unwrapped(v1, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .
